{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1515185596,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyODY0MDIwODA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2063","origin":"github"},"title":"ENH: datalad shell  command","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nwhile thinking about #2062 I though that it might be nice to have a simple `datalad shell` command which would by default simply start a new shell session, but it could provide superpowers\n- `--auto` option would enable AutomagicIO, at least for the sub-processes which import datalad (hence could be activated using env var #2062). Eventually an implementation providing overrides for basic syscalls and thus more of FUSE like functionality could be provided\n- `-d DS` would just cd to that dataset directory, so it is more of \"pushd/popd\" tandem\n- `--record-runs` - if we could pull off to use `datalad run` for any command executed, might be quite cool! VCS controlled shell all the way down\n- anything else (shell aliases of some kind? ;) )","files":null}]}